# Scripts stay local — they hold keys, one-off jobs and scraped data. The exceptions are the two
# that carry no secrets and exist to keep D1 agreeing with the rules in lib/: the lead sourcing CLI,
# lost twice with the sourcing rules inside it, and the area reclassifier, whose absence turns the
# next change to AREAS into a hand-written migration restating every ZIP range. Written as
# `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/`, because git does not descend into an excluded directory and
# a negation under one never matches.
scripts/*
!scripts/get-leads.ts
!scripts/reclassify-areas.ts
docs/
# Scraped lead data — real businesses with phone numbers and addresses. The generator writes one
# file per area (seed-leads-fort-lauderdale.sql and friends), so match the whole family.
d1/seed-leads*.sql
d1/seed-demo-pool.sql
# Generated from the live table, so it carries the same real phone numbers as a seed file.
d1/backfill-zip.sql
# One-off output of scripts/reclassify-areas.ts, regenerated whenever AREAS changes.
d1/reclassify-areas.sql
# Working notes, internal specs, sales material — anything that stays off the remote
/local/
